            <ArticleTitle>Contained rupture of mycotic aneurysm of the left circumflex coronary artery in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/2150135114551994</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery aneurysm (CAA) is defined as dilatation of a coronary artery segment to a diameter of more than 1.5-fold normal size. Rupture of CAA is a catastrophic event and may result in sudden death or myocardial infarction. We report this unusual case of contained rupture of the left circumflex CAA.</AbstractText>
